{"skill":{"slug":"web-perf","displayName":"Web Perf"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767685545091,"changelog":"Initial release of the web-perf skill – a web performance audit tool powered by Chrome DevTools MCP. \n\n- Audits Core Web Vitals (FCP, LCP, TBT, CLS, Speed Index) and provides detailed breakdowns.\n- Identifies render-blocking resources, network dependency chains, and caching issues.\n- Spots high-level accessibility gaps with a snapshot tool.\n- Offers workflow and tool usage checklist for step-by-step auditing.\n- Includes clear output formatting and actionable, prioritized recommendations.\n- Guides analysis of codebase optimizations when source code is available; otherwise audits third-party sites externally.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":7621,"sha256":"dbb0e6ab3e3565cf49de6b2c3bcd62339aafebb099514ec3c86771a096cd920b","contentType":"text/x-markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2260,"sha256":"5f4289ad56439bbc8dcdd2e24ee9f53a43d09e61bfa8682783a8608651ea1d3b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789015005509,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"4ec32bae58cb670371fae795600d232240206ea7b0141cfdc9a953c18563c73d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/4ec32bae58cb670371fae795600d232240206ea7b0141cfdc9a953c18563c73d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: web-perf\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious primarily due to the 'Phase 5: Codebase Analysis' section in `SKILL.md`. This section instructs the AI agent to 'Search for configuration files' (e.g., `webpack.config.js`, `package.json`). While this action is plausibly related to web performance analysis, it implicitly instructs the agent to access and read local files. If the agent possesses file system access capabilities, this constitutes a high-risk behavior, even without clear malicious intent for exfiltration or unauthorized modification. Additionally, the `SKILL.md` recommends the user configure their environment by running `npx -y chrome-devtools-mcp@latest`, which introduces a supply chain risk as `npx -y` downloads and executes the latest version of a package without explicit confirmation, though this is a user setup instruction, not an agent action.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159647688},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789015005509},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is coherent for web performance auditing, but its setup asks users to run a mutable third-party MCP package locally via npx without pinning a reviewed version.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Browser instrumentation and network/page inspection are proportionate for performance auditing, but a local MCP server may have access to the user's browser context and local environment depending on how it is run.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The MCP setup block instructs users to configure a local command using npx with -y and chrome-devtools-mcp@latest, which can download and execute a changing third-party package after review.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The instructions are task-scoped and do not include prompt hijacking, memory writes, credential collection, destructive actions, or unrelated behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact does not install persistence or background services itself, but adding the MCP entry to user configuration creates a durable local tool integration until the user removes it.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill's stated purpose is web performance auditing with Chrome DevTools MCP, and its runtime workflow stays focused on page navigation, performance traces, network analysis, accessibility snapshots, and optional codebase inspection.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable adding a local Chrome DevTools MCP server. Prefer pinning chrome-devtools-mcp to a specific reviewed version, avoid auto-confirming installs where practical, and run the MCP server with the least local and browser access needed for the audit.","findings":"[T08] unexpected: The artifact confirms the flagged setup pattern at SKILL.md lines 16-20: a local MCP command invokes npx -y with chrome-devtools-mcp@latest. This is purpose-related but not necessary to be unpinned or auto-confirmed, so it remains a material review concern.\n[SkillSpector] expected: SkillSpector reported no issues; independent inspection found no embedded scripts, hidden instructions, exfiltration, or destructive behavior in the skill markdown.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789015005509}}}}}